	/// Opaque, URL-safe opponent ID; clients must not parse it. Derived server-side from the whole (unfiltered) archive, so filters never change it. Form 1, 'uscf-<USCF member ID>': used when the opponent's matched Games carry exactly one USCF member ID and no other Opponent name carries that same ID (strictly unambiguous, as in ADR 0007). It survives a Chapter-header rename of the opponent. Form 2, 'name-<base64url without padding of the UTF-8 Opponent name, trimmed>': every other opponent. Reversible, so it needs no lookup table and cannot collide. The server must keep resolving a name- ID after the opponent later gains a USCF match (decode it and look up the name), so a client's saved ID never breaks; responses always carry the current canonical ID. Games with a blank Opponent name have no opponent ID and are never listed.
